UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/2332432.2332449
N1  - Abstract is from the authors' extended 2015 arXiv version (arXiv:1512.08943); the cited 2012 conference abstract is two pages.
AB  - Reconfigurable state machine replication is an important enabler of elasticity for replicated cloud services, which must be able to dynamically adjust their size as a function of changing load and resource availability. We introduce a new generic framework to allow a reconfigurable state machine implementation to be derived from arbitrary non-reconfigurable state machines. It allows speculative command execution to ensure uninterrupted progress during reconfiguration, even when failures delay agreement. We apply the framework to non-reconfigurable Paxos and evaluate it on a distributed testbed.
KW  - consensus
